# Vue component conventions

- Use Vue 3 Composition API and TypeScript.
- Primary two-way value uses `modelValue` and `update:modelValue`.
- Prefer slots over props that pass renderable UI fragments.
- Reuse shared `size`, `radius`, `color`, `variant` and polymorphic types when available.
- Avoid exposing DOM/internal implementation state as public API.
- Keep state logic in composables when it is reusable by more than one component.
- Emit meaningful user-facing events only.
- Preserve native HTML semantics when a native element can express the behavior.
- Use stable `data-*` state attributes when consumers need styling hooks.
